    M=[2, 3, 5, 8]     mu=  4/17 kappa=  3/13 gap=0.0045  [2odd+2even]
    M=[2, 5, 7, 12]    mu=  9/37 kappa=  4/17 gap=0.0079  [2odd+2even]

  READING: the parity signature of the combinatorial class -- is '4odd+0even'
  or the balanced '2odd+2even' (the Liu-Zhu composite signature) over-represented?

====================================================================================================
  FOCUSED: Liu-Zhu family M={x,y,y-x,y+x} -- both-odd (composite) vs x=1 (generic)
====================================================================================================
    (x,y)=(1,5) M=[1, 4, 5, 6]     [2odd+2even] mu=   2/9 kappa=   2/9  SLAB (mu=kappa)  (x=1)
    (x,y)=(3,5) M=[2, 3, 5, 8]     [2odd+2even] mu=  4/17 kappa=  3/13  COMBINATORIAL (mu>kappa)  (both-odd)
    (x,y)=(1,7) M=[1, 6, 7, 8]     [2odd+2even] mu=  3/13 kappa=  3/13  SLAB (mu=kappa)  (x=1)
    (x,y)=(3,7) M=[3, 4, 7, 10]    [2odd+2even] mu=  6/25 kappa=  4/17  COMBINATORIAL (mu>kappa)  (both-odd)
    (x,y)=(5,7) M=[2, 5, 7, 12]    [2odd+2even] mu=  9/37 kappa=  4/17  COMBINATORIAL (mu>kappa)  (both-odd)
    (x,y)=(1,9) M=[1, 8, 9, 10]    [2odd+2even] mu=  4/17 kappa=  4/17  SLAB (mu=kappa)  (x=1)
    (x,y)=(5,9) M=[4, 5, 9, 14]    [2odd+2even] mu= 12/49 kappa=  3/13  COMBINATORIAL (mu>kappa)  (both-odd)
    (x,y)=(7,9) M=[2, 7, 9, 16]    [2odd+2even] mu= 16/65 kappa=  6/25  COMBINATORIAL (mu>kappa)  (both-odd)

  CONCLUSION: x=1 (M has signature 2odd+2even but y-x=y-1, y+x=y+1 straddle a
  slab-compatible residue pattern) => slab; both-odd x>=3 => combinatorial.
  The small-gcd/composite structure is where the ROTATION (uniform tool) breaks
  -- the Motzkin-side mirror of mac-mini-S56's density-floor observation.
